# Exercise 3 – Network Traffic Analysis Using Wireshark

## Objective
To capture and analyze network packets using Wireshark
and understand how application-layer information can be
exposed through unencrypted network traffic.

## Tool Used
- Wireshark

## Description
Wireshark is a network protocol analyzer used to capture,
inspect and analyze network traffic.

This experiment was performed in a controlled lab environment
for educational purposes.

## Procedure
1. Open Wireshark.
2. Select the appropriate network interface.
3. Start packet capture.
4. Generate network traffic in the controlled lab.
5. Stop the capture.
6. Apply suitable display filters.
7. Inspect packet headers and protocol information.
8. Analyze the captured traffic.

## Result
Network packets were successfully captured and analyzed using
Wireshark.

## Security Observation
Unencrypted protocols can expose sensitive information during
transmission. Encrypted protocols such as HTTPS should be used
to protect credentials and sensitive data.

